\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{An eigenvalue on the imaginary axis}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The Morris–Lecar foci of \ref{fnip-0037} and the FitzHugh–Nagumo
focus of \ref{fnip-0038} are [hyperbolic](fnip-0034): every
eigenvalue has nonzero real part, and \ref{fnip-0043} applies. The
saddle and the node of \ref{fnip-0047} are hyperbolic as well.}

\p{A [Jacobian](fnip-0034) can also have an eigenvalue of real part
zero. The homeomorphism of \ref{fnip-0043} is stated for a
hyperbolic equilibrium, and this eigenvalue is the remaining case.}
